t absorption, while also being susceptible to various diseases that can impact its function.\",8\r\n12387,ENFERMEDADES INFLAMATORIAS INTESTINALES,\"Enfermedades Inflamatorias Intestinales son condiciones que afectan el tubo digestivo, requiriendo atención médica y nutricional especial. Estas enfermedades pueden provocar desnutrición y déficits de micronutrientes, lo que subraya la importancia de un manejo adecuado y un enfoque integral en su tratamiento.\",10\r\n4997,MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL,\"The \"\"MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL\"\" refers to the complex community of microorganisms residing in the human digestive tract, which plays a vital role in health and disease. This intestinal microbiota is crucial for various metabolic processes, including energy absorption, appetite regulation, and the maintenance of the immune system. It has been identified as a key factor in the development of metabolic disorders such as obesity and diabetes.\n\nResearch indicates that the composition and variations of the intestinal microbiota can significantly differ between Western and Eastern populations, influenced by dietary patterns. Diets rich in animal protein can alter the microbiota's composition, highlighting the relationship between diet and microbial communities in the gut. Additionally, the microbiota undergoes significant changes during early life, influenced by factors such as the method of birth and dietary intake.\n\nOverall, the intestinal microbiota is essential for energy homeostasis and has profound implications for human health, particularly in relation to metabolic conditions.\",44\r\n12091,DISBIOSIS,\"DISBIOSIS refers to an imbalance in the gut microbiota, which can lead to various health issues and diseases in both children and adults. Probiotics are often used to correct this imbalance, aiming to improve health outcomes. The condition is associated with a range of diseases, highlighting the importance of maintaining a healthy gut microbiome for overall well-being.\",14\r\n8978,LACTOBACILLUS,\"Lactobacillus is a genus of bacteria that resides in the gastrointestinal tract and is widely recognized for its numerous health benefits, particularly in relation to digestive health. This genus is commonly utilized as probiotics, which are live microorganisms that confer health advantages when consumed in adequate amounts. Lactobacillus is known for its ability to ferment lactose and produce lactic acid, contributing to gut health and the maintenance of a positive metabolic profile.\n\nResearch has indicated that Lactobacillus may have beneficial effects on obesity and metabolic health, making it a subject of interest in studies related to these areas. Additionally, Lactobacillus can ferment undigested carbohydrates into D-lactic acid, which may lead to complications in certain patients, such as those with short bowel syndrome (SIC). The growth and activity of Lactobacillus can be enhanced by prebiotic fibers, further supporting its role in promoting gut health.\n\nOverall, Lactobacillus is a significant type of beneficial bacteria within the phylum Firmicutes, playing a crucial role in fermentation processes and contributing positively to digestive and metabolic health.\",14\r\n8980,BACTEROIDES,\"Bacteroides is a genus of bacteria that plays a crucial role in the human gut, particularly in the digestion of complex carbohydrates. It is predominantly found in the intestines and is part of the phylum Bacteroidetes. Research has shown that Bacteroides is negatively associated with obesity, suggesting that its presence may be linked to healthier weight management. Interestingly, this genus has also been found to increase in individuals who successfully lose weight. Additionally, Bacteroides is more prevalent in the intestinal microbiota of African children, which is associated with diets rich in plant fiber. Overall, Bacteroides is essential for digestive health and may influence body weight regulation.\",8\r\n9033,BUTIRATO,\"Butirato, also known as butyrate, is a short-chain fatty acid produced by gut bacteria during the fermentation of dietary fiber. It plays a crucial role in energy metabolism by providing energy to colon epithelial cells and reducing intestinal permeability. Additionally, butirato is involved in the apoptosis of inflammatory cells and enhances the function of the mucosal barrier, contributing to inflammation reduction and overall gut health.\",5\r\n8982,CLOSTRIDIUM,\"Clostridium is a genus of bacteria within the phylum Firmicutes, encompassing species that can be either beneficial or pathogenic in the human intestine. This genus has been associated with various health implications, including its role in gut health and disease. Notably, certain species of Clostridium have been linked to obesity and metabolic alterations, highlighting their impact on metabolic health. Overall, Clostridium plays a complex role in the human gut, contributing to both beneficial functions and potential pathogenic effects.\",4\r\n8999,EUBACTERIUM,\"Eubacterium is a genus of bacteria that plays a significant role in metabolic health and obesity. It is part of the normal gut flora and is involved in various metabolic processes essential for maintaining gut health. Eubacterium belongs to the phylum Firmicutes, highlighting its importance in the overall functioning of the gastrointestinal system.\",3\r\n8979,STREPTOCOCCUS,\"Streptococcus is a genus of bacteria belonging to the phylum Firmicutes. These bacteria are commonly found in the gastrointestinal tract and play a significant role in human health and microbiota. Streptococcus can have both beneficial and pathogenic effects, highlighting its dual nature in the context of human health.\",3\r\n9000,FUSOBACTERIUM,\"Fusobacterium is a genus of bacteria that belongs to the phylum Fusobacteria. It is commonly found as part of the normal flora in the human mouth and gut. While many species of Fusobacterium coexist harmlessly within these environments, some are associated with various diseases. This dual role highlights the complexity of Fusobacterium, as it can contribute to both health and disease states in humans.\",2\r\n9006,NIÑOS AFRICANOS,\"Grupo de niños que presentan una microbiota intestinal rica en Bacteroidetes y con una mayor riqueza microbiana en comparación con los niños europeos, debido a su dieta alta en fibra y baja en grasas animales.\",2\r\n9007,NIÑOS EUROPEOS,\"Grupo de niños que presentan una microbiota intestinal caracterizada por una mayor proporción de Firmicutes y una menor riqueza microbiana, atribuida a su dieta alta en grasas y proteínas de origen animal y baja en fibra.\",2\r\n9044,RECEPTOR TOLL-LIKE 4,\"TLR4 is a receptor that recognizes lipopolysaccharides from gram-negative bacteria, activating inflammatory pathways.\",2\r\n9043,ACIDOS BILIARES,\"Bile acids are produced in the liver and play a role in fat digestion and metabolism, with primary and secondary forms affecting energy expenditure.\",1\r\n5000,ACIDOS GRASOS DE CADENA CORTA,\"Short-chain fatty acids (SCFA) are fermentation products derived from dietary fiber, playing significant roles in energy metabolism and the reduction of inflammation. They are produced during the fermentation process of dietary fiber by the intestinal microbiota, highlighting their importance in gut health and overall metabolic functions.\",1\r\n9008,DIETA ALTA EN FIBRA,Patrón dietético que se asocia con un aumento en la proporción de Bacteroidetes y una disminución en Firmicutes en la microbiota intestinal.,1\r\n9013,DIETA ALTA EN GRASAS,,1\r\n8994,ELDERMET,\"ELDERMET is a consortium that studies the microbiota of the elderly, finding distinct characteristics compared to younger adults.\",1\r\n8996,ENTEROBACTERIACEAE,\"Enterobacteriaceae is a family of bacteria within the phylum Proteobacteria, commonly found in the intestines and important for gut flora.\",1\r\n8995,FILO: BACTEROIDETES,Filo: Bacteroidetes is another major phylum of bacteria that plays a crucial role in the composition of the intestinal microbiota.,1\r\n9005,FILO: FIRMICUTES,,1\r\n8987,INTESTINO GRUESO,El intestino grueso es la parte del tracto gastrointestinal donde reside la mayor cantidad de bacterias y se lleva a cabo la absorción de agua y electrolitos.,1\r\n9011,MICROBIOTA DE COMUNIDADES OCCIDENTALES,\"Descripción de la microbiota intestinal de comunidades occidentales, caracterizada por una ingesta alta en grasa y proteínas de origen animal y un bajo contenido en fibra.\",1\r\n9012,MICROBIOTA DE COMUNIDADES ORIENTALES,\"Descripción de la microbiota intestinal de comunidades orientales, que muestra una mayor riqueza microbiana y una mayor proporción de Bacteroidetes.\",1\r\n8986,TRACTO GASTROINTESTINAL,El tracto gastrointestinal es el sistema de órganos que se encarga de la digestión y absorción de nutrientes en el cuerpo humano.,1\r\n8998,VEILLONELLA,\"Veillonella is a genus of bacteria within the phylum Firmicutes, known for its role in the human microbiome.\",1\r\n9001,PEPTOSTREPTOCOCCUS,\"Peptostreptococcus is a genus of bacteria within the phylum Firmicutes, significant in the context of human health.\",1\r\n9002,RUMINOCOCCUS,\"Ruminococcus is a genus of bacteria belonging to the phylum Firmicutes. This genus is recognized for its significant role in the fermentation of dietary fibers, contributing to the digestive processes in various organisms. Additionally, Ruminococcus has been associated with decreased amounts in obese individuals, suggesting a potential link between its presence and body weight regulation.\",1\r\n9010,PATRONES DIETÉTICOS,\"Factores que influyen en la composición de la microbiota intestinal, mostrando diferencias significativas entre grupos con hábitos dietéticos diferentes.\",1\r\n9045,PROBIOTICOS,Probiotics are beneficial bacteria that can modulate gut microbiota composition and enhance butyrate production.,1\r\n9056,POLISACÁRIDOS INDIGERIBLES,\"Indigestible polysaccharides are substances that require microbiota to convert 